From: Jeffrey Benjamin Brown <jeffbrown.the@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] Fix disconnect loop when the poll probe falls back to select

The working-poll configure test calls open(), but does not include the header
that declares it.  Modern compilers reject the implicit declaration under
-Werror, causing a false negative and selecting event_loop/select.c even on
Linux systems with a working poll().

Include fcntl.h so the intended poll backend is selected.  Also make the
select fallback leave its event loop when libmonome reports a read error;
select's exceptional descriptor set does not reliably report a tty hangup,
while the readable set remains ready at EOF and otherwise causes a CPU spin.
---
 src/serialosc-device/event_loop/select.c | 5 +++--
 wscript                                  | 1 +
 2 files changed, 4 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/serialosc-device/event_loop/select.c b/src/serialosc-device/event_loop/select.c
index 785f2ee..5ac9910 100644
--- a/src/serialosc-device/event_loop/select.c
+++ b/src/serialosc-device/event_loop/select.c
@@ -83,8 +83,9 @@ sosc_event_loop(struct sosc_state *state)
 			return 1;
 
 		/* is there data available for reading from the monome? */
-		if (FD_ISSET(monome_fd, &rfds))
-			monome_event_handle_next(state->monome);
+		if (FD_ISSET(monome_fd, &rfds)
+				&& monome_event_handle_next(state->monome) < 0)
+			break;
 
 		/* how about from OSC? */
 		if (FD_ISSET(osc_fd, &rfds))
diff --git a/wscript b/wscript
index 71ee80e..caf5829 100644
--- a/wscript
+++ b/wscript
@@ -21,6 +21,7 @@ def check_poll(conf):
 
 	code = """
 		#include <stdlib.h>
+		#include <fcntl.h>
 		#include <poll.h>
 
 		int main(int argc, char **argv) {
-- 
